WEBVTT


00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.231
Swannie.


00:01:54.305 --> 00:01:56.280
Come over here.


00:01:57.953 --> 00:01:59.382
Come to me.


00:02:02.753 --> 00:02:04.695
Nice, Swan.


00:02:10.081 --> 00:02:11.870
Come on.


00:02:11.937 --> 00:02:14.007
Come to me,
Mr. Swan.


00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:16.697
You'll frighten it!


00:02:20.802 --> 00:02:22.395
Help!


00:02:25.154 --> 00:02:26.583
Help!


00:02:27.778 --> 00:02:29.403
Go get my parents.
Go!


00:02:51.457 --> 00:02:52.984
I've killed him.


00:02:53.057 --> 00:02:55.479
I've killed him.


00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:58.394
I kill...


00:02:58.465 --> 00:03:00.854
ohh.


00:03:03.585 --> 00:03:05.789
Ohh.


00:03:09.281 --> 00:03:10.525
Nathan!


00:03:14.433 --> 00:03:16.059
Oh Jesus.


00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:17.340
- Where's Claire?
- Call 911!


00:03:17.409 --> 00:03:19.481
- I don't know what happened!
- Where is she?


00:03:19.553 --> 00:03:22.849
- He came out of nowhere!
- Nathan...


00:03:22.913 --> 00:03:25.052
Do you think he can hear me?


00:03:26.113 --> 00:03:28.001
Where's Claire?


00:03:28.065 --> 00:03:29.559
Where is she?


00:03:29.633 --> 00:03:31.258
I'll look for her later!


00:04:13.313 --> 00:04:14.807
I was dead.


00:04:14.881 --> 00:04:17.532
I mean,


00:04:17.601 --> 00:04:19.608
I was really dead.


00:04:19.681 --> 00:04:21.405
Really.


00:04:24.225 --> 00:04:25.502
<i>Tell me about it.</i>


00:04:25.569 --> 00:04:27.063
<i>What's it like to be dead?</i>


00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:31.959
I'd got loose.


00:04:33.729 --> 00:04:37.275
It were as if I was
getting out of my body.


00:04:38.785 --> 00:04:42.201
My body was
staying here, and I...


00:04:42.273 --> 00:04:43.997
I was flying.


00:04:46.018 --> 00:04:48.156
<i>You were floating?</i>


00:04:49.569 --> 00:04:50.911
Yes.


00:04:50.978 --> 00:04:53.498
I heard that dog,
and a woman screaming.


00:04:53.569 --> 00:04:56.252
They were around me,
panicking and...


00:04:56.321 --> 00:04:59.321
then I heard that noise.


00:04:59.393 --> 00:05:01.662
It was like a whistle.


00:05:01.729 --> 00:05:04.599
A very, very loud whistle.


00:05:05.633 --> 00:05:09.211
I saw... a light.


00:05:09.281 --> 00:05:10.296
<i>A light?</i>


00:05:12.161 --> 00:05:13.787
Yes.


00:05:15.361 --> 00:05:17.466
It was alive.


00:05:17.537 --> 00:05:20.886
It was alive
as if it were waiting for me.


00:05:22.177 --> 00:05:24.544
I was in the light.


00:05:24.609 --> 00:05:26.398
I felt good.


00:05:26.465 --> 00:05:29.432
- Didn't you want to come back?
- No.


00:05:29.505 --> 00:05:31.709
<i>But you did come back.</i>


00:05:31.777 --> 00:05:33.021
Yes.


00:05:34.657 --> 00:05:36.664
<i>Why did you come back?</i>


00:05:38.529 --> 00:05:40.601
I just did.


00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:43.128
<i>Something made you come back.</i>


00:05:43.201 --> 00:05:45.590
Is there something you're holding back?


00:05:47.841 --> 00:05:50.230
Yes.


00:05:51.521 --> 00:05:53.528
Hey, would you like
to hear about Jesus Christ?


00:05:53.601 --> 00:05:55.608
Here you go.


00:06:00.481 --> 00:06:02.685
Would you like to hear


00:06:02.753 --> 00:06:05.241
Excuse me, would you like to hear
about Jesus Christ today?


00:06:05.313 --> 00:06:06.491
Like to hear about Jesus Christ?


00:06:06.562 --> 00:06:07.871
- Okay.
- Thank you very much, sir.


00:06:07.937 --> 00:06:09.497
Would you like to hear about Jesus Christ?
Have a great day.


00:06:09.569 --> 00:06:12.603
Would you like to hear
about Jesus Christ today?


00:06:37.409 --> 00:06:39.962
<i>But what made him come back?</i>


00:06:40.033 --> 00:06:42.651
Won't you answer?


00:06:43.681 --> 00:06:45.437
Nathan?


00:06:50.273 --> 00:06:52.313
<i>... right turn.</i>


00:06:54.369 --> 00:06:55.579
<i>It doesn't recover.</i>


00:06:57.793 --> 00:06:59.703
<i>We're dropping the...</i>


00:07:01.409 --> 00:07:03.482
<i>Speed, 220 knots.</i>


00:07:05.249 --> 00:07:07.388
<i>Wings lowered.</i>


00:07:09.185 --> 00:07:11.225
<i>Flap up.</i>
<i>Flap up! Flap up!</i>


00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:13.271
<i>Power! Power!</i>


00:07:13.345 --> 00:07:15.255
<i>Oh, shit!</i>


00:07:16.833 --> 00:07:18.743
<i>No!</i>


00:07:30.209 --> 00:07:33.056
Of the 45 passengers on board,


00:07:33.121 --> 00:07:35.608
nine belonged
to the same family.


00:07:35.681 --> 00:07:36.761
All from Haiti.


00:07:37.921 --> 00:07:39.546
So?


00:07:39.617 --> 00:07:42.105
So they're afraid of getting fucked over
by the Warsaw Convention.


00:07:42.177 --> 00:07:44.217
I explained to them
that doesn't exist here,


00:07:44.289 --> 00:07:45.598
but they're scared,
even still.


00:07:45.665 --> 00:07:47.126
They set up a committee.


00:07:47.201 --> 00:07:48.728
I met their spokesman.


00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:50.295
They gave me this.


00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:51.929
What does the NTSB say about this?


00:07:52.001 --> 00:07:53.146
The NTSB isn't getting involved.


00:07:53.217 --> 00:07:54.624
Neither is the FAA.


00:07:54.689 --> 00:07:56.413
They've all washed their hands of it.


00:07:56.481 --> 00:07:58.390
The airline is registered
in the Virgin Islands,


00:07:58.465 --> 00:07:59.927
the tour operator in the Caymans.


00:08:00.001 --> 00:08:01.943
The crew is from Russia.
They still don't know


00:08:02.017 --> 00:08:04.221
if the plane crashed in Haiti
or the Dominican Republic.


00:08:04.289 --> 00:08:05.664
Every day it's a different story.


00:08:05.729 --> 00:08:08.151
But the plane was due
to land here in the US?


00:08:08.225 --> 00:08:09.403
Seems like everyone forgot that.


00:08:09.473 --> 00:08:11.710
The FAA isn't going
to go poking its nose in.


00:08:11.777 --> 00:08:14.646
Too much work, too much hassle,
too much everything.


00:08:19.617 --> 00:08:20.795
Nathan?


00:08:20.865 --> 00:08:23.832
I don't like the smell of it.


00:08:23.905 --> 00:08:25.498
If the FAA won't get involved,


00:08:25.569 --> 00:08:28.089
that means a lawsuit like this
could drag on for years.


00:08:28.161 --> 00:08:30.266
That means hundreds
of thousands of dollars.


00:08:30.337 --> 00:08:33.206
And it means we can forget
about the Hague Protocol.


00:08:33.281 --> 00:08:35.289
I don't like it.


00:08:35.361 --> 00:08:37.249
Excuse me,


00:08:37.313 --> 00:08:40.248
since when are we afraid of cases
that drag on for years?


00:08:40.321 --> 00:08:42.295
These people are going
to get fucked over


00:08:42.369 --> 00:08:43.831
on the pretext that no convention...


00:08:43.905 --> 00:08:46.654
It was the same shit in Unterlinguen.


00:08:46.721 --> 00:08:48.096
In Kinshasa too.


00:08:48.161 --> 00:08:51.194
A judge will show up
with his calculator and say what?


00:08:51.265 --> 00:08:53.436
"All right, let's imagine
some two-year-old kid


00:08:53.505 --> 00:08:54.999
"who has lost his mother.


00:08:55.073 --> 00:08:56.283
"We'll say she'd have devoted


00:08:56.353 --> 00:08:58.971
how much of her time
to him, per day?"


00:08:59.041 --> 00:09:01.048
- Michael?
- Three hours, tops.


00:09:01.121 --> 00:09:03.161
That's a good mother.


00:09:04.705 --> 00:09:06.429
Up until the age of 18,


00:09:06.497 --> 00:09:10.904
which gives us three hours
a day, times 365 days,


00:09:10.977 --> 00:09:13.181
times $8 an hour,


00:09:13.249 --> 00:09:15.005
plus the usual interest...


00:09:15.073 --> 00:09:17.375
that totals a little less


00:09:17.441 --> 00:09:19.296
than $100,000 at best.


00:09:19.361 --> 00:09:21.500
- And the plane wasn't even full.
- See?


00:09:21.569 --> 00:09:23.260
How far will that get you?


00:09:23.329 --> 00:09:26.711
You can't even take your mistress
on a weekend trip.


00:09:26.785 --> 00:09:27.767
Nothing.


00:09:27.841 --> 00:09:31.157
All right, fine.
But tomorrow morning,


00:09:31.233 --> 00:09:33.306
these people are going
to be in my office.


00:09:33.377 --> 00:09:35.962
- What do you want me to tell them?
- Send them to me.


00:09:36.033 --> 00:09:38.586
I'll explain everything.
They'll understand, don't worry.


00:09:40.737 --> 00:09:42.461
Anything else?


00:10:04.865 --> 00:10:07.647
Your appointment is here.


00:10:07.713 --> 00:10:09.306
Who is this guy?
Remind me.


00:10:09.377 --> 00:10:10.359
Joseph Kay.


00:10:10.433 --> 00:10:12.059
Heads up a department at St. Louis.


00:10:12.129 --> 00:10:14.681
- I'm not sure what he wants.
- Heads up a department?


00:10:14.752 --> 00:10:16.029
Something like that.


00:10:16.097 --> 00:10:17.046
"Something like that."


00:10:17.121 --> 00:10:18.201
"I'm not sure what he wants."


00:10:18.273 --> 00:10:19.582
What's that supposed to mean?


00:10:19.649 --> 00:10:21.340
Why send him to me?


00:10:21.409 --> 00:10:23.548
- You were recommended.
- By who?


00:10:24.545 --> 00:10:26.433
- Who upstairs?
- Ross.


00:10:27.553 --> 00:10:28.982
I see.


00:10:37.121 --> 00:10:38.711
- Your daughter called.
- Oh, yeah?


00:10:38.785 --> 00:10:40.640
She left you messages at home and...


00:10:40.705 --> 00:10:42.047
Yeah, I know.
I forgot.


00:10:42.113 --> 00:10:44.185
She wanted to talk
about the vacation.


00:10:44.257 --> 00:10:46.526
She wanted to know,
was it, "Like the usual?"


00:10:46.593 --> 00:10:49.048
This was my daughter
who called or my wife?


00:10:49.121 --> 00:10:50.201
Your daughter.


00:10:51.425 --> 00:10:53.214
Okay, I'll call her back.


00:11:00.929 --> 00:11:02.206
Yes?


00:11:02.273 --> 00:11:03.964
All that glucose...


00:11:04.033 --> 00:11:05.527
Yes?


00:11:05.601 --> 00:11:07.324
Worries me.


00:11:09.472 --> 00:11:11.131
I can examine you if you want.


00:11:11.201 --> 00:11:12.542
I'm a doctor.


00:11:14.113 --> 00:11:15.226
All right...


00:11:15.297 --> 00:11:17.184
what can I do for you, Dr. Kay?


00:11:17.249 --> 00:11:18.526
You work at St. Louis, right?


00:11:18.593 --> 00:11:20.054
I don't know if I'm the right...


00:11:20.129 --> 00:11:22.464
Nathan, I believe you
have misunderstood me.


00:11:22.529 --> 00:11:23.576
I'm very serious.


00:11:23.649 --> 00:11:25.918
You mustn't take
hypoglycemia lightly.


00:11:25.985 --> 00:11:29.760
In fact, you shouldn't
take any symptom lightly... ever.


00:11:29.825 --> 00:11:32.695
You can't imagine the number
of cells you burn up every day.


00:11:32.768 --> 00:11:34.427
Of course, you'll tell me
you're also manufacturing...


00:11:34.497 --> 00:11:36.504
- I don't want to interrupt...
- But it's not so.


00:11:36.577 --> 00:11:38.813
Neurons can't be replaced.
Some die every day.


00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:40.255
Every day a few more.


00:11:40.321 --> 00:11:43.965
All that glucose you're pumping in
is just cheap energy.


00:11:44.032 --> 00:11:46.683
Very bad for you,
very bad for the neurons.


00:11:46.753 --> 00:11:50.583
Thank you for your concern
about my health, but I'm fine.


00:11:50.656 --> 00:11:53.723
Now why don't you tell me
what you want from me?


00:11:55.649 --> 00:11:57.307
That slight shaking in your hands,


00:11:57.376 --> 00:11:59.132
have you had that a long time?


00:11:59.201 --> 00:12:00.891
It's a morning thing, right?


00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:02.237
When you wake up?


00:12:02.305 --> 00:12:05.917
You work too much.


00:12:05.985 --> 00:12:06.912
Sure.


00:12:06.976 --> 00:12:09.082
Excuse me.


00:12:11.041 --> 00:12:12.699
Oui, mon ange.


00:12:12.769 --> 00:12:14.874
Yes, sweetheart, I know.


00:12:15.873 --> 00:12:17.531
Yeah, yeah.


00:12:17.601 --> 00:12:19.575
Daddy will call you back,
but now I'm...


00:12:19.649 --> 00:12:21.373
wait, hang on.


00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:25.496
Would you excuse me a second?


00:12:26.497 --> 00:12:27.806
Yeah?


00:12:27.873 --> 00:12:29.880
Uh-huh.


00:12:31.105 --> 00:12:33.407
Honey, I can't talk to you now.


00:12:33.473 --> 00:12:36.539
Rachel, check out
that guy for me... now.


00:12:36.609 --> 00:12:38.397
Of course you're coming for vacation.


00:12:38.465 --> 00:12:40.253
Sure you are.


00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:41.913
No, honey, I can't come get you.


00:12:41.984 --> 00:12:44.373
We'll do just like last time, I...


00:12:44.449 --> 00:12:46.686
We'll see.


00:12:46.753 --> 00:12:49.273
Okay, I'll call you back.
Love you.


00:12:49.345 --> 00:12:51.800
Don't ever do this to me again.
Ever.


00:12:51.873 --> 00:12:53.564
I've got a screwball in my office.


00:12:53.633 --> 00:12:55.640
He may be a screwball,
but he wasn't lying.


00:12:55.713 --> 00:12:57.502
He's head of a department at St. Louis.


00:12:58.816 --> 00:13:00.027
Ross didn't tell you anything else?


00:13:00.097 --> 00:13:01.274
No, nothing.


00:13:10.784 --> 00:13:13.206
They say the swan sings only once,


00:13:13.281 --> 00:13:14.742
just before dying.


00:13:14.817 --> 00:13:15.799
Yes, I know.


00:13:15.873 --> 00:13:18.426
He senses he's going to die,
so he sings.


00:13:18.497 --> 00:13:20.155
It's not because of the pain.


00:13:20.225 --> 00:13:22.527
On the contrary,
he sings because he's glad.


00:13:22.593 --> 00:13:24.186
He's glad to die.


00:13:24.257 --> 00:13:26.712
- The number of legends about swans...
- Dr. Kay.


00:13:26.785 --> 00:13:28.672
They also say swans


00:13:28.737 --> 00:13:31.071
guide and keep company
with the dead,


00:13:31.137 --> 00:13:33.046
to help them cross the threshold.


00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:35.641
That's my favorite...
a very old Celtic legend.


00:13:35.713 --> 00:13:37.207
- Yes, I know it.
- You do?


00:13:37.281 --> 00:13:40.183
- Yes, my wife told me about it.
- Your wife told you about it?


00:13:40.257 --> 00:13:41.685
Right.


00:13:42.913 --> 00:13:44.604
You mean your ex-wife?


00:13:46.497 --> 00:13:48.155
We all live in glass houses.


00:13:50.273 --> 00:13:52.128
So I see.


00:13:52.193 --> 00:13:54.680
Why don't you finally tell me
what I can do for you?


00:13:54.752 --> 00:13:57.600
I believe I'm the one
who can do something for you.


00:13:57.665 --> 00:13:59.192
But you'll see for yourself.


00:13:59.265 --> 00:14:01.883
Certain experiences
can be very unsettling.


00:14:01.953 --> 00:14:04.735
I'll see what, for God's sake?
What experiences?


00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:08.575
I'm merely pointing out
the need to be prepared.


00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:10.648
Is that a threat?


00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:12.444
No, it's not a threat.


00:14:12.513 --> 00:14:14.138
It's a message.


00:14:14.208 --> 00:14:17.111
But I'm not quite sure
you're ready to hear it.


00:14:18.752 --> 00:14:20.694
How come you know
so much about me?


00:14:20.768 --> 00:14:22.295
Did you have me checked out?
Did you...


00:14:22.369 --> 00:14:24.474
was it Ross
told you all that stuff?


00:14:24.545 --> 00:14:26.749
"The need to be prepared."
What's that supposed to mean?


00:14:26.817 --> 00:14:28.344
I don't know this Ross person.


00:14:28.417 --> 00:14:29.726
I've never met the guy.


00:14:30.368 --> 00:14:32.473
And I think you know
what I want from you.


00:14:33.248 --> 00:14:34.623
I think you know very well.


00:15:55.937 --> 00:15:57.660
Hello?


00:15:57.728 --> 00:15:59.255
<i>It's me.</i>


00:16:01.185 --> 00:16:02.559
<i>Claire, hello.</i>


00:16:02.944 --> 00:16:04.439
Yeah, I'm here.


00:16:05.281 --> 00:16:06.557
<i>Is Tracey there?</i>


00:16:07.201 --> 00:16:08.662
Yeah, sure.
You want to talk to her?


00:16:08.737 --> 00:16:11.323
She called me today.
She wanted me to call back.


00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:13.531
I know, she told me.


00:16:16.064 --> 00:16:19.839
Um, Tracey's asleep.
She's in bed.


00:16:19.904 --> 00:16:22.173
Already? Is she okay?
What's wrong?


00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:25.502
<i>She waited for you to call all day.</i>


00:16:25.568 --> 00:16:28.023
She's drawing things
I don't understand


00:16:28.096 --> 00:16:29.503
and waking up at night.


00:16:30.401 --> 00:16:31.710
No, she's not okay.


00:16:31.777 --> 00:16:34.559
Is there anything I can do?


00:16:39.745 --> 00:16:42.974
Let's talk about this
another time, okay?


00:16:43.041 --> 00:16:44.383
I'll tell her you called.


00:16:44.449 --> 00:16:45.943
Okay.


00:17:26.785 --> 00:17:28.311
Nathan.


00:17:29.313 --> 00:17:31.768
Nathan!
Nathan.


00:17:31.841 --> 00:17:35.256
Listen, I came to apologize
for this morning.


00:17:35.329 --> 00:17:38.744
I was a little heavy-handed
and I wanted to apologize.


00:17:38.817 --> 00:17:41.664
I have something to show you
not far from here.


00:17:41.728 --> 00:17:42.656
Nathan, wait.
Listen.


00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:44.247
I have something to show you,


00:17:44.321 --> 00:17:47.070
I just don't know if you'll be able
to handle it, that's all.


00:17:47.136 --> 00:17:49.624
I'm fed up with your mysteries.
I'm tired.


00:17:49.696 --> 00:17:51.703
Nathan, it'll take
five minutes of your time,


00:17:51.776 --> 00:17:53.598
no more.
And then I'm out of here.


00:17:53.665 --> 00:17:56.152
You'll never see me again.
I give you my word.


00:17:56.224 --> 00:17:57.980
- You give me your word?
- Yes.


00:17:58.817 --> 00:18:00.726
I give you my word.
You know who I am,


00:18:00.801 --> 00:18:02.743
you know where I work,
you're a lawyer.


00:18:02.817 --> 00:18:05.915
If I do anything wrong,
anything at all which...


00:18:05.984 --> 00:18:09.694
It wouldn't take you five minutes
to blow my career out of the water.


00:18:09.760 --> 00:18:12.630
Nathan, believe me,
it's important.


00:18:12.704 --> 00:18:13.850
You have to see it.


00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:15.709
I swear.


00:18:16.353 --> 00:18:19.167
It's important.
Come with me.


00:18:21.824 --> 00:18:24.726
Five minutes.
10 minutes... no more.


00:18:24.801 --> 00:18:26.873
And then... I'm gone.


00:18:34.208 --> 00:18:36.891
You brought me here
just to tell me this?


00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:38.040
What the hell does it mean?


00:18:38.112 --> 00:18:40.022
Or is that all part of the message?


00:18:40.097 --> 00:18:42.039
You come out with these
little riddles of yours


00:18:42.112 --> 00:18:43.771
and expect me to...


00:18:44.353 --> 00:18:47.386
You see that guy,
the kid in the orange jacket?


00:18:47.456 --> 00:18:48.438
Do you see him?


00:18:48.512 --> 00:18:50.422
Yeah, I see him.
So what?


00:18:50.496 --> 00:18:53.082
Name of Dennis.
10 years ago to this day,


00:18:53.152 --> 00:18:54.494
his father died here.


00:18:54.561 --> 00:18:58.455
He was waiting for a train
as he did every evening.


00:18:58.528 --> 00:19:01.212
He had a good job, happy family.


00:19:01.281 --> 00:19:05.339
And one evening, he'd had enough.


00:19:05.408 --> 00:19:07.896
And when the express came by,
he jumped.


00:19:07.968 --> 00:19:09.430
Was he a friend of yours?


00:19:10.113 --> 00:19:11.706
And these last few days,


00:19:11.777 --> 00:19:14.297
Dennis has come here
every evening.


00:19:14.369 --> 00:19:16.605
- Every evening.
- Do you ever answer a question?


00:19:16.672 --> 00:19:18.495
Look at him.


00:19:18.561 --> 00:19:20.416
- Why should I?
- Look at him.


00:19:20.481 --> 00:19:23.961
Because in about two minutes,


00:19:24.032 --> 00:19:27.862
Dennis there will be dead.


00:19:27.936 --> 00:19:29.016
What the f...


00:19:36.352 --> 00:19:37.399
You're crazy.


00:19:37.472 --> 00:19:39.479
Completely crazy.


00:19:57.313 --> 00:20:00.127
You gotta take the Chambers Street Exit,
right across the platform.


00:20:17.760 --> 00:20:18.905
Look!


00:20:18.976 --> 00:20:20.056
He's got a gun!


00:20:20.128 --> 00:20:22.845
He's got a gun!
He's got a gun!


00:20:22.912 --> 00:20:24.854
Listen, don't do it!


00:20:24.928 --> 00:20:26.903
Please,
put the gun down!


00:21:59.776 --> 00:22:01.118
Is this your first time?


00:22:02.688 --> 00:22:05.590
You seem kind of young.


00:22:09.408 --> 00:22:10.870
He's here to see Dr. Kay.


00:22:10.944 --> 00:22:13.311
- Okay.
- He'll come get you in the day room.


00:22:13.376 --> 00:22:14.686
- This way?
- Mm-hmm.


00:22:14.752 --> 00:22:17.403
I... I think what you're
doing is wonderful.


00:22:50.272 --> 00:22:52.159
You came to see him?


00:22:53.280 --> 00:22:56.128
He'll be here.
Just have to wait.


00:22:59.424 --> 00:23:01.049
Come here.


00:23:03.360 --> 00:23:05.334
Come here.


00:23:05.408 --> 00:23:07.797
What's the matter?


00:23:07.872 --> 00:23:09.530
Something wrong?


00:23:13.152 --> 00:23:15.803
Myocardial metastases.


00:23:16.800 --> 00:23:18.174
Cancer of the heart muscle.


00:23:18.240 --> 00:23:19.996
Super rare, right?


00:23:21.152 --> 00:23:23.421
They wrote an article
about me in a magazine.


00:23:23.488 --> 00:23:26.008
It's in my room,
if you want to see it.


00:23:26.080 --> 00:23:32.026
Apparently, I could croak
from one day to the next...


00:23:32.096 --> 00:23:35.675
from one minute to the next.


00:23:37.344 --> 00:23:40.640
- Jeremy.
- Nathan.


00:23:40.704 --> 00:23:42.013
What do you do, Nathan?


00:23:42.080 --> 00:23:44.927
I'm a lawyer.
Do you know if he's going to be long?


00:23:44.992 --> 00:23:48.854
The first doc I saw,
you know what he called it?


00:23:49.792 --> 00:23:52.410
"Hypertrophic cardiomyopathy."


00:23:52.480 --> 00:23:54.236
Wow.


00:23:54.304 --> 00:23:56.671
Can you believe that guy?


00:23:58.624 --> 00:24:00.926
You and me,


00:24:00.992 --> 00:24:02.553
we're gonna slap that that son-of-a-bitch
with a lawsuit.


00:24:02.624 --> 00:24:03.606
What do you say?


00:24:03.680 --> 00:24:05.786
Legally, that's not exactly my bag.


00:24:05.857 --> 00:24:07.351
Jeremy, hello.


00:24:07.424 --> 00:24:09.977
- Up already?
- Yeah.


00:24:10.048 --> 00:24:12.437
- Happy birthday.
- Yeah, thanks.


00:24:12.512 --> 00:24:15.065
You've made a new friend.


00:24:15.136 --> 00:24:17.111
- Are you the new volunteer?
- He's a lawyer.


00:24:17.952 --> 00:24:19.774
He and I are gonna throw
a doctor's ass in the slammer.


00:24:19.840 --> 00:24:23.615
Oh, well... see you later.


00:24:24.864 --> 00:24:26.074
Bye.


00:24:32.352 --> 00:24:34.261
You smell that stink?


00:24:35.872 --> 00:24:37.497
Like something's rotting?


00:24:37.568 --> 00:24:39.673
Behind the stink of detergent...


00:24:39.744 --> 00:24:41.337
can't you smell that?


00:24:42.560 --> 00:24:45.375
It reeks of death around here.


00:24:45.440 --> 00:24:47.993
Why do you think she puts up with it?


00:24:49.280 --> 00:24:52.728
She had a kid who died.
That's why.


00:24:54.208 --> 00:24:58.616
All of us in here
are going out in body bags,


00:24:58.688 --> 00:25:00.062
and she knows that.


00:25:01.728 --> 00:25:05.820
She thinks that when we see
her little darling up there


00:25:05.888 --> 00:25:07.349
we'll tell him
how mommy's doing.


00:25:07.424 --> 00:25:09.082
And we'll take care of him.


00:25:09.152 --> 00:25:13.375
Make sure he eats his dinner
and goes to the potty up in Heaven.


00:25:13.440 --> 00:25:15.928
Volunteer, my ass.


00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:17.527
What about you?


00:25:17.600 --> 00:25:19.488
You got a message to send, too?


00:25:19.552 --> 00:25:21.046
Who you got up there, huh?


00:25:22.496 --> 00:25:25.464
I'm going soon,
so make the most of it.


00:25:26.912 --> 00:25:29.181
Some "dearly beloved?"


00:25:29.248 --> 00:25:31.037
- Or maybe...
- Excuse me.


00:25:31.104 --> 00:25:32.511
Hey!


00:25:32.576 --> 00:25:33.688
Hey, come back.


00:25:33.760 --> 00:25:36.313
I didn't mean it like that.


00:25:44.960 --> 00:25:48.124
I don't know how to die.


00:25:48.192 --> 00:25:50.101
None of us know how to die.


00:25:52.192 --> 00:25:55.738
But maybe...


00:25:55.808 --> 00:25:58.655
somewhere deep inside of us


00:25:58.720 --> 00:26:00.378
a part of us does know how.


00:26:00.448 --> 00:26:05.369
Maybe it's not as terrible
as it seems.


00:26:05.440 --> 00:26:07.993
Try and rest.


00:26:10.688 --> 00:26:14.100
You know, Nathan,
the dying have taught me one thing...


00:26:14.176 --> 00:26:17.176
that you can look death in the face
and go on living.


00:26:17.248 --> 00:26:19.615
Our mission here is
to keep them company.


00:26:19.680 --> 00:26:22.069
Keep company with those
about to die


00:26:22.144 --> 00:26:24.086
so that they can depart in peace.


00:26:24.160 --> 00:26:26.680
Great, but what's it
got to do with me?


00:26:26.752 --> 00:26:27.799
Me, my.


00:26:27.872 --> 00:26:29.301
My little consciousness,


00:26:29.376 --> 00:26:31.961
my little comforts,
my little life.


00:26:32.031 --> 00:26:36.123
What about others, Nathan,
do you ever think about them?


00:26:36.192 --> 00:26:39.290
And Dennis?
Have you thought about Dennis?


00:26:39.360 --> 00:26:41.334
If you knew he was going
to blow his brains out,


00:26:41.408 --> 00:26:42.488
why didn't you do something?


00:26:42.560 --> 00:26:44.894
Why didn't you try to listen to him?


00:26:44.960 --> 00:26:47.164
Who kept Dennis company
so he'd "depart in peace?"


00:26:47.232 --> 00:26:50.494
Anyway, how did you know
he was going to die?


00:26:50.560 --> 00:26:52.251
This time I want an answer,
none of your...


00:26:52.320 --> 00:26:53.880
- I saw it.
- You saw it?


00:26:53.952 --> 00:26:55.294
- Yes.
- How did you see it?


00:26:55.360 --> 00:26:57.182
Was it written on his face?


00:26:57.248 --> 00:26:59.614
- Yes.
- Yes?


00:26:59.680 --> 00:27:02.549
Listen, I'm beat.
I didn't sleep last night because of you,


00:27:02.624 --> 00:27:04.991
- and I've got to be at work...
- Nathan,


00:27:05.056 --> 00:27:06.071
people who come here,


00:27:06.144 --> 00:27:09.210
they've already traveled
a long road


00:27:09.280 --> 00:27:11.003
paved with suffering.


00:27:11.072 --> 00:27:13.919
But they have had time
to prepare themselves.


00:27:15.040 --> 00:27:17.145
But often death comes...


00:27:17.216 --> 00:27:19.223
unexpectedly.
It can't be predicted.


00:27:19.296 --> 00:27:20.408
Yes, I know, yes.


00:27:20.480 --> 00:27:24.026
For instance, say you cross
the street at the wrong moment,


00:27:24.096 --> 00:27:27.063
or the body just gives out...
just like that.


00:27:27.136 --> 00:27:28.794
Snap your fingers,
you're dead.


00:27:28.864 --> 00:27:30.239
We see that every day.


00:27:30.304 --> 00:27:33.533
And those people never have
time to untangle the knots.


00:27:33.600 --> 00:27:36.535
They never have time
to prepare themselves.


00:27:36.607 --> 00:27:37.622
And so?


00:27:37.696 --> 00:27:39.736
And so...


00:27:40.736 --> 00:27:44.217
the role of the Messengers
is to give those people too


00:27:44.287 --> 00:27:46.654
a chance to be reconciled.


00:27:46.720 --> 00:27:48.923
- "The Messengers?"
- Yes.


00:27:53.631 --> 00:27:55.290
I don't understand.


00:27:55.360 --> 00:27:58.077
There are people out there
who know in advance


00:27:58.144 --> 00:28:00.151
that someone is going to die.


00:28:00.224 --> 00:28:02.875
Let's say they...
"got the message."


00:28:02.944 --> 00:28:04.766
And in those cases,


00:28:04.832 --> 00:28:09.240
their job is to help that person
depart in peace... reconcile.


00:28:09.312 --> 00:28:11.613
- And you're one of these "Messengers?"
- Yes, I am.


00:28:11.680 --> 00:28:13.338
- You know who's going to die?
- Yes.


00:28:13.408 --> 00:28:15.263
- You see it?
- Yes, I see it.


00:28:15.328 --> 00:28:17.597
And you help them depart in peace.


00:28:18.656 --> 00:28:21.590
Nathan, I realize it
may be hard to believe...


00:28:21.664 --> 00:28:24.053
But Dennis didn't depart in peace.


00:28:25.056 --> 00:28:26.300
- No.
- Why?


00:28:26.368 --> 00:28:29.019
We don't always succeed.
Sometimes we get there too late.


00:28:29.088 --> 00:28:31.292
No one has power over
the hour of death.


00:28:31.360 --> 00:28:32.287
No one.


00:28:33.408 --> 00:28:35.317
I don't believe you.


00:28:35.392 --> 00:28:37.399
Have it your way, Nathan.


00:28:37.472 --> 00:28:39.294
But these things can still exist


00:28:39.359 --> 00:28:41.301
whether you believe
in them or not.


00:28:42.336 --> 00:28:45.565
I know when someone's
going to die... I see it.


00:28:45.632 --> 00:28:49.494
And I make every effort
to prepare them for what's coming.


00:28:50.400 --> 00:28:52.287
Well, I think I've
heard enough for today.


00:29:16.351 --> 00:29:18.653
What exactly are you
trying to tell me?


00:29:19.935 --> 00:29:23.864
Are you trying to tell me
I'm going to die soon? Is that it?


00:29:23.936 --> 00:29:27.929
I told you everything.
You know everything.


00:29:28.000 --> 00:29:29.593
Go fuck yourself.


00:29:49.248 --> 00:29:50.654
Hurry up.


00:29:50.720 --> 00:29:53.567
Sam.
Sam, hurry up.


00:29:54.560 --> 00:29:56.764
Bring that over.
Hurry up.


00:29:56.832 --> 00:29:58.009
Breathe, breathe,
breathe.


00:29:58.079 --> 00:30:01.308
We need a neck brace and a splint.
Get that here.


00:31:11.424 --> 00:31:14.588
Look straight into the light.


00:31:14.656 --> 00:31:15.736
Don't move.


00:32:01.567 --> 00:32:03.225
The smell of the ghosts.


00:32:03.295 --> 00:32:06.143
Follow the smell of the ghosts
and you'll find the flower.


00:32:06.208 --> 00:32:08.412
<i>What did you say, sweetheart?</i>


00:32:08.480 --> 00:32:09.625
It's a cactus.


00:32:09.696 --> 00:32:12.085
It makes a flower once a year,
at midnight.


00:32:12.160 --> 00:32:13.589
Only once.


00:32:13.664 --> 00:32:16.511
At 12:00 noon, the flower dies,
and it smells like ghosts.


00:32:16.575 --> 00:32:18.430
The flower smells like ghosts?


00:32:18.495 --> 00:32:19.575
<i>Yeah,</i>
<i>but it's real nice.</i>


00:32:19.648 --> 00:32:21.503
Mommy says ghosts smell good.


00:32:21.568 --> 00:32:23.804
<i>The Night Blooming Cereus.</i>
<i>Yes, I remember.</i>


00:32:23.872 --> 00:32:25.432
<i>Mommy told me about it too.</i>


00:32:25.504 --> 00:32:27.576
An Indian legend.


00:32:27.647 --> 00:32:29.371
Honey, can I talk to Mommy?


00:32:29.440 --> 00:32:31.895
<i>She says she'll call you back.</i>


00:32:31.968 --> 00:32:34.139
Tracey?


00:32:34.207 --> 00:32:35.734
Hello?


00:32:40.319 --> 00:32:42.326
I had everything checked out,
everything...


00:32:42.399 --> 00:32:44.985
brain, heart, lungs, blood.


00:32:45.056 --> 00:32:47.390
I got my urine tested,
my saliva, my sperm...


00:32:47.455 --> 00:32:49.016
they tested everything


00:32:49.088 --> 00:32:50.233
and they found nothing.


00:32:50.304 --> 00:32:51.929
Nothing at all.
There's the file.


00:32:51.999 --> 00:32:53.243
Take a look.


00:32:53.311 --> 00:32:55.450
A little hypoglycemia
and nothing else.


00:32:55.520 --> 00:32:56.665
Nothing else at all.


00:32:57.984 --> 00:32:59.511
I'm very glad to hear that, Nathan.


00:32:59.583 --> 00:33:01.372
- I'm happy for you.
- So as of this minute,


00:33:01.439 --> 00:33:02.649
you are out of my life.


00:33:02.719 --> 00:33:04.759
No phone calls,
no visits, nothing.


00:33:04.831 --> 00:33:07.613
If I ever see you again
here or any place at all,


00:33:07.680 --> 00:33:09.273
it'll mean the police...
got it?


00:33:09.344 --> 00:33:10.805
May I show you something?


00:33:10.880 --> 00:33:12.789
- No.
- It's a photograph.


00:33:13.952 --> 00:33:16.057
Anna Rachevsky.


00:33:16.128 --> 00:33:17.404
Very cute.
Now leave.


00:33:17.471 --> 00:33:18.878
From a Russian family.


00:33:18.944 --> 00:33:22.042
That photograph was taken
the day she arrived in New York.


00:33:22.111 --> 00:33:23.769
I don't give a shit.


00:33:24.416 --> 00:33:26.390
Not much money,
father out of the picture.


00:33:26.463 --> 00:33:28.798
She wanted to go to college,
but the closest she ever got


00:33:28.864 --> 00:33:31.253
was working in
the cafeteria at NYU.


00:33:32.063 --> 00:33:34.365
Her boss treated her
like an animal.


00:33:34.431 --> 00:33:36.220
The students didn't even notice.


00:33:37.279 --> 00:33:38.261
Except one.


00:33:38.335 --> 00:33:40.888
He was a foreigner too...


00:33:41.759 --> 00:33:43.003
a Frenchman.


00:33:43.935 --> 00:33:46.139
She welcomed the kindness
he showed her.


00:33:46.656 --> 00:33:48.379
But later, she was fired.


00:33:48.447 --> 00:33:50.869
He lost touch with her.


00:33:50.944 --> 00:33:52.286
End of story.


00:33:55.136 --> 00:33:57.624
Anna Rachevsky, right.


00:33:57.695 --> 00:33:59.354
- Coming back?
- Yes.


00:33:59.424 --> 00:34:02.806
She works at the Greenwind diner
in Queens.


00:34:02.879 --> 00:34:03.861
Late night shift.


00:34:03.936 --> 00:34:05.627
Not very well paying.


00:34:06.175 --> 00:34:08.957
She's had a child...
a son.


00:34:10.015 --> 00:34:12.055
You should stop by and see her.


00:34:12.127 --> 00:34:14.844
I'm sure she would
enjoy that very much.


00:34:14.911 --> 00:34:16.700
I'll do that, maybe, yes.


00:34:16.768 --> 00:34:17.946
Good.


00:34:19.615 --> 00:34:20.859
What?


00:34:22.112 --> 00:34:23.770
Have you understood me?


00:34:23.840 --> 00:34:25.301
No.


00:34:26.560 --> 00:34:27.607
What?


00:34:28.224 --> 00:34:29.685
What was it this time?
What did you see?


00:34:29.759 --> 00:34:31.898
Tell me.
A blinking light?


00:34:31.968 --> 00:34:33.756
Some kind of Christmas tree
that begins to...


00:34:33.823 --> 00:34:35.230
No, actually, Nathan,


00:34:35.296 --> 00:34:37.849
it's a bright white light
that surrounds the person.


00:34:37.920 --> 00:34:39.446
But that's not the most
important thing.


00:34:39.519 --> 00:34:41.853
What's the most important thing?


00:34:41.920 --> 00:34:45.269
The most important thing
is suddenly you'll just know.


00:34:46.399 --> 00:34:49.247
You'll know she's going to die.


00:35:23.552 --> 00:35:25.112
Nathan?


00:35:26.751 --> 00:35:28.311
What are you doing here?


00:35:28.991 --> 00:35:30.006
Doing?
Well, I...


00:35:30.080 --> 00:35:31.738
I'm just here.


00:35:32.896 --> 00:35:35.165
You're as handsome as ever.


00:35:37.215 --> 00:35:38.393
Well?


00:35:38.464 --> 00:35:40.536
What? No, I just...


00:35:40.607 --> 00:35:42.746
actually I was passing through.


00:35:42.816 --> 00:35:44.060
You doing okay?


00:35:44.447 --> 00:35:45.974
You were passing through here?


00:35:46.559 --> 00:35:48.795
Yes, I was going back
to the city.


00:35:48.864 --> 00:35:51.165
I was in Queens
and I was going home.


00:35:51.231 --> 00:35:54.614
I was dying for a cup of coffee,
and here I am.


00:35:54.688 --> 00:35:56.117
You go heavy
on the sugar, huh?


00:35:56.192 --> 00:35:58.101
Yes. You're looking well.


00:35:59.775 --> 00:36:01.815
- What?
- I said you're looking well.


00:36:01.887 --> 00:36:03.098
How's your health?
Okay?


00:36:03.168 --> 00:36:05.502
You look like you're
in fine health.


00:36:05.567 --> 00:36:06.777
Yes, fine.


00:36:08.703 --> 00:36:10.907
It's strange for me,
seeing you again.


00:36:10.975 --> 00:36:13.048
Excuse me.


00:36:32.447 --> 00:36:34.552
- Are you married?
- Divorced.


00:36:34.623 --> 00:36:35.900
Oh.


00:36:35.968 --> 00:36:37.823
I never had the time.


00:36:37.888 --> 00:36:39.644
He walked out before marrying me.


00:36:39.711 --> 00:36:42.777
He still found the time
to knock me up first though.


00:36:43.263 --> 00:36:45.532
A good thing too,
you might say.


00:36:45.599 --> 00:36:46.810
A little boy.


00:36:50.560 --> 00:36:52.086
- What's this?
- It's for you.


00:36:52.159 --> 00:36:54.428
These are my numbers.
This one...


00:36:54.495 --> 00:36:56.568
is the direct line
to Rachel, my assistant,


00:36:56.639 --> 00:36:58.046
and that's my cell phone.


00:36:58.111 --> 00:37:00.533
And don't hesitate to...


00:37:00.607 --> 00:37:01.916
if you need me for anything,


00:37:01.984 --> 00:37:04.122
if anything should come up,


00:37:04.191 --> 00:37:05.817
call me. Okay?


00:37:05.887 --> 00:37:08.472
If anything comes up,
I call you.


00:37:09.087 --> 00:37:10.429
Okay.


00:37:11.743 --> 00:37:13.531
And what could possibly come up?


00:37:14.655 --> 00:37:17.525
- How old is your daughter?
- Seven.


00:37:18.239 --> 00:37:19.898
Do you speak French with her?


00:37:19.968 --> 00:37:21.910
- No, not much.
- You should.


00:37:21.983 --> 00:37:23.161
I know.


00:37:23.839 --> 00:37:26.173
Look at me,
I hardly speak Russian anymore.


00:37:26.240 --> 00:37:28.760
But when my father came back,
he talked and talked.


00:37:28.831 --> 00:37:30.489
He wouldn't stop talking.


00:37:30.559 --> 00:37:33.341
- Did I tell you my father came back?
- No.


