00:54:33.288 --> 00:54:35.459
It's probable...
indeed very probable...


00:54:35.528 --> 00:54:38.943
that Paul was a victim
of Sudden Infant Death Syndrome.


00:54:39.016 --> 00:54:42.399
It's the most
mysterious cause of death.


00:54:43.336 --> 00:54:46.183
The most mysterious,
the most arbitrary...


00:54:46.248 --> 00:54:47.874
and the most cruel.


00:54:49.480 --> 00:54:50.975
You're angry and that's normal.


00:54:51.048 --> 00:54:52.707
Let's leave my anger out of this.


00:54:52.777 --> 00:54:56.933
Someone didn't do his job
and an innocent child is dead.


00:54:57.000 --> 00:54:57.928
That's the reality.


00:54:57.992 --> 00:54:59.967
There is no mystery.


00:55:00.040 --> 00:55:01.950
An inexplicable death?


00:55:02.024 --> 00:55:03.682
I don't know
what that means.


00:55:03.752 --> 00:55:04.996
It doesn't exist.


00:55:05.064 --> 00:55:07.617
It's just a way to cover up
someone's incompetence.


00:55:07.688 --> 00:55:09.695
I see it every day.


00:55:13.416 --> 00:55:16.897
If you would like,
there is a procedure...


00:55:16.968 --> 00:55:20.035
Perhaps the only one
that allows us to rule out


00:55:20.105 --> 00:55:21.217
the most common hypothesis.


00:55:21.288 --> 00:55:22.848
Out of the question.


00:55:23.976 --> 00:55:24.958
You can take some time
and think about it.


00:55:25.032 --> 00:55:27.585
No.
No autopsy.


00:55:27.656 --> 00:55:29.314
Out of the question.


00:55:30.728 --> 00:55:32.637
I forbid you to touch my son.


00:55:42.920 --> 00:55:45.887
Why some are victims,
why others are not is...


00:56:06.632 --> 00:56:08.323
<i>"Dear Jennifer,</i>


00:56:08.392 --> 00:56:11.840
<i>"I'd like to talk to you</i>
<i>about these long nights when I'm alone.</i>


00:56:11.912 --> 00:56:15.556
<i>"About the nighttime crossings...</i>


00:56:15.624 --> 00:56:18.821
<i>"desert crossings filled with ghosts.</i>


00:56:19.752 --> 00:56:21.061
<i>"And about these hearts I hear</i>


00:56:21.128 --> 00:56:23.201
<i>"beating deep inside all these rooms...</i>


00:56:24.968 --> 00:56:27.456
<i>"deep inside all these bodies,</i>


00:56:27.528 --> 00:56:30.528
<i>"these hearts that want to go on beating</i>
<i>and don't give up.</i>


00:56:33.288 --> 00:56:38.110
<i>"They say life is worth living,</i>
<i>and they want more of it.</i>


00:56:42.088 --> 00:56:43.746
<i>My heart hasn't given up either. "


00:56:48.488 --> 00:56:50.397
I know it's hard for you.


00:56:50.472 --> 00:56:52.359
I know what all this has cost you,


00:56:52.424 --> 00:56:54.082
what a stay in a hospital costs...


00:56:54.728 --> 00:56:57.030
And I know that
with your night job you...


00:56:57.096 --> 00:56:58.340
No, Nathan.


00:56:59.368 --> 00:57:00.448
It's kind of you.


00:57:00.520 --> 00:57:02.243
I'd just like to help.
It's not much,


00:57:02.312 --> 00:57:04.614
but at least you wouldn't
have to worry about money.


00:57:04.680 --> 00:57:06.371
That's all.
I can do that, at least.


00:57:06.440 --> 00:57:07.902
No.


00:57:10.280 --> 00:57:12.647
<i>"Here, they all believe in God.</i>


00:57:15.848 --> 00:57:17.190
<i>"But me,</i>


00:57:17.256 --> 00:57:20.605
<i>"I believe in this</i>
<i>beating heart of mine</i>


00:57:20.680 --> 00:57:23.135
<i>"and this pulsing in my veins.</i>


00:57:23.208 --> 00:57:25.215
<i>"I believe in this force</i>
<i>inside of me.</i>


00:57:27.432 --> 00:57:30.466
<i>"If you come to see me,</i>
<i>I'll tell you about my life here,</i>


00:57:30.536 --> 00:57:33.405
<i>"about those times the fear rises up</i>
<i>and lifts you so high...</i>


00:57:33.480 --> 00:57:36.230
<i>"...it makes you feel dizzy.</i>


00:57:37.640 --> 00:57:40.423
<i>"Hopelessness too.</i>


00:57:40.488 --> 00:57:42.343
<i>"You go through these moments</i>


00:57:42.408 --> 00:57:44.677
<i>"and think you're gone,</i>
<i>and you tremble.</i>


00:57:46.696 --> 00:57:49.030
<i>"But sometimes...</i>


00:57:49.096 --> 00:57:51.300
<i>"yes, sometimes...</i>
<i>you discover within yourself</i>


00:57:51.368 --> 00:57:53.278
<i>"an unsuspected strength.</i>


00:57:54.728 --> 00:57:56.353
<i>"You'll see all this strength...</i>


00:57:56.424 --> 00:57:59.141
<i>"you will...</i>
<i>if you come to see me.</i>


00:58:04.328 --> 00:58:06.913
<i>"I know I'm gonna die soon.</i>


00:58:06.984 --> 00:58:09.537
<i>"And I know I'm here</i>
<i>to learn something.</i>


00:58:17.864 --> 00:58:20.319
<i>"When I've learned what I've</i>
<i>come to learn,</i>


00:58:20.392 --> 00:58:23.523
<i>"I'll go.</i>
<i>I know that.</i>


00:58:27.784 --> 00:58:29.988
<i>"But in my head,</i>


00:58:30.056 --> 00:58:32.674
<i>I can't imagine</i>
<i>that life comes to an end. "


00:58:43.816 --> 00:58:47.231
Hi, Nathan, this is Anna.


00:58:47.304 --> 00:58:48.100
Am I bothering you?


00:58:48.168 --> 00:58:49.379
<i>No, not at all.</i>


00:58:49.448 --> 00:58:50.430
<i>How are you?</i>


00:58:50.504 --> 00:58:51.910
I, um...


00:58:51.976 --> 00:58:53.950
I've been thinking
about your offer


00:58:54.024 --> 00:58:57.253
and I think I'm going to accept it.


00:58:57.320 --> 00:58:59.295
<i>Good. I'll call my bank right away.</i>


00:58:59.368 --> 00:59:00.677
- <i>Okay?</i>
<i>- Yes.</i>


00:59:07.208 --> 00:59:08.801
I didn't understand you, angel.


00:59:08.872 --> 00:59:10.148
What did you say?


00:59:10.216 --> 00:59:11.906
<i>There was a storm last night.</i>


00:59:11.976 --> 00:59:13.984
Really?


00:59:14.056 --> 00:59:15.430
<i>Yeah.</i>


00:59:15.496 --> 00:59:18.845
- Well, what was it like?
- <i>I saw lightning.</i>


00:59:18.920 --> 00:59:20.643
Honey, I can't stay
on the phone too long.


00:59:20.712 --> 00:59:21.574
- <i>Daddy?</i>
- Yes.


00:59:21.640 --> 00:59:23.974
I don't want to go
on the plane by myself.


00:59:24.040 --> 00:59:25.982
Why, honey?
What's wrong?


00:59:26.056 --> 00:59:27.845
<i>I want you to come</i>
<i>and get me.</i>


00:59:27.912 --> 00:59:29.254
You won't be alone.


00:59:29.320 --> 00:59:30.432
There will be somebody
to keep you company.


00:59:30.504 --> 00:59:32.064
That's the way we've
always done it.


00:59:32.136 --> 00:59:34.144
- But I'm scared.
- <i>You're scared?</i>


00:59:34.216 --> 00:59:36.933
What are you scared of, sweetie?
There's no reason...


00:59:37.000 --> 00:59:39.334
<i>I'm scared of taking</i>
<i>the plane by myself.</i>


00:59:39.400 --> 00:59:41.375
<i>I'm scared of storms.</i>


00:59:41.448 --> 00:59:43.749
- <i>I'm scared of lightning.</i>
- Do It.


00:59:43.816 --> 00:59:45.376
- <i>Daddy?</i>
- Yes?


00:59:45.448 --> 00:59:48.197
<i>I want you to come and get me.</i>


00:59:48.264 --> 00:59:50.565
Sir, want to come with me please?


00:59:50.631 --> 00:59:51.809
- What for?
- Sir, please.


00:59:51.880 --> 00:59:55.263
- Get the fuck away from me, okay?
- Honey, I have to go.


00:59:55.336 --> 00:59:57.539
- Honey. Honey. I'll call you back.
- Leave me alone, all right?


00:59:57.608 --> 00:59:59.647
- Not yet.
- Sir, you need to come with me...


00:59:59.720 --> 01:00:01.695
Or what?


01:00:01.768 --> 01:00:04.256
Asshole, what are you going to do now?
What now?


01:00:04.328 --> 01:00:06.400
All you get down!


01:00:31.752 --> 01:00:33.607
Anna, can you hear me?


01:00:34.216 --> 01:00:35.110
Anna.


01:00:36.136 --> 01:00:37.991
Anna.


01:00:42.856 --> 01:00:44.100
- Are you okay?
- Call someone.


01:00:44.168 --> 01:00:47.168
Call someone.
Anna.


01:01:31.496 --> 01:01:32.576
<i>Hello?</i>


01:01:32.647 --> 01:01:34.240
<i>It's Anna.</i>


01:01:34.311 --> 01:01:36.384
I know.


01:01:36.456 --> 01:01:37.666
<i>Listen, where are you?</i>


01:01:37.736 --> 01:01:39.460
<i>I'll call come and pick you up.</i>


01:01:39.528 --> 01:01:41.535
- No.
- <i>Tell me where you are... please.</i>


01:01:41.608 --> 01:01:43.463
How much time do I have left?


01:01:43.528 --> 01:01:44.705
Tell me when.


01:01:44.775 --> 01:01:46.848
<i>Nathan, the time</i>
<i>you have left is your own.</i>


01:01:46.920 --> 01:01:49.505
Tell me how long.
Just tell me.


01:01:49.575 --> 01:01:51.102
I don't know.


01:01:51.176 --> 01:01:52.899
<i>Don't give me that.</i>


01:01:52.968 --> 01:01:54.429
You knew for the others.


01:01:54.504 --> 01:01:56.391
So tell me when.


01:01:56.456 --> 01:01:59.522
All I can do is help.


01:01:59.592 --> 01:02:01.185
Nathan, tell me where you are.


01:02:55.656 --> 01:02:57.566
May I come in?


01:02:57.639 --> 01:03:00.836
I went to see them...


01:03:00.904 --> 01:03:02.693
the Rachevskys.


01:03:04.488 --> 01:03:06.277
I wanted to tell them


01:03:06.344 --> 01:03:08.166
she died because of me.


01:03:09.544 --> 01:03:11.846
If I hadn't taken her
to that bank,


01:03:11.912 --> 01:03:14.181
she'd still be here with us.


01:03:15.144 --> 01:03:17.184
Her son would still have a mother.


01:03:19.303 --> 01:03:21.725
But I didn't even have
that much courage.


01:03:26.056 --> 01:03:27.681
Do you remember
when you called me


01:03:27.751 --> 01:03:30.053
from the hospital that day?


01:03:31.239 --> 01:03:33.574
You said you'd saved her?
You were wrong.


01:03:34.344 --> 01:03:36.613
Today you say you killed her,
you're still wrong.


01:03:36.680 --> 01:03:40.837
With or without you,
Anna would've died.


01:03:40.904 --> 01:03:44.482
In her father's place,
or a couple of hours later


01:03:44.552 --> 01:03:46.756
falling down a flight of stairs.


01:03:46.824 --> 01:03:48.515
No one knows.


01:03:48.584 --> 01:03:50.274
- No one can know.
- I don't want to die.


01:03:50.344 --> 01:03:52.678
- Nathan...
- I don't want to die.


01:03:52.744 --> 01:03:53.540
I'll say it again.


01:03:53.608 --> 01:03:57.186
No one has power
over the hour of death.


01:04:03.496 --> 01:04:04.608
Hello?


01:04:04.679 --> 01:04:06.654
<i>It's me.</i>


01:04:06.728 --> 01:04:08.451
<i>I want you</i>
<i>to come and see me.</i>


01:04:08.519 --> 01:04:10.210
<i>I want you to come right away...</i>
<i>both of you.</i>


01:04:10.280 --> 01:04:11.557
What's going on?


01:04:11.624 --> 01:04:13.249
<i>It's nothing.</i>


01:04:13.319 --> 01:04:16.319
You must come...
both of you.


01:04:16.392 --> 01:04:19.294
- Nathan, what's the matter?
- <i>Nothing.</i>


01:04:19.368 --> 01:04:21.343
- <i>You can tell me.</i>
- Yeah, sure.


01:04:21.415 --> 01:04:23.488
I'll be okay.


01:04:23.560 --> 01:04:24.934
I just wanted to see you.


01:04:24.999 --> 01:04:27.421
I'm sorry,
I'll call you later.


01:04:27.496 --> 01:04:28.957
<i>You gonna be okay?</i>


01:04:29.031 --> 01:04:29.980
Yeah.


01:04:30.055 --> 01:04:31.517
<i>Are you sure?</i>


01:04:31.592 --> 01:04:33.567
Yeah, sure.


01:04:33.639 --> 01:04:35.428
<i>I'm sorry.</i>


01:04:42.216 --> 01:04:44.933
<i>Paul was dead and...</i>


01:04:44.999 --> 01:04:47.236
I just screamed at her...


01:04:48.968 --> 01:04:50.823
as if she was to blame.


01:04:53.095 --> 01:04:56.194
You never talked to her
about it afterwards?


01:04:56.263 --> 01:04:58.085
No.


01:04:59.080 --> 01:05:00.324
She was right to leave.


01:05:00.392 --> 01:05:02.050
They're both happy.
That's good.


01:05:06.248 --> 01:05:08.517
She always had
a mind of her own.


01:05:09.255 --> 01:05:12.387
Yes.
Always.


01:05:12.456 --> 01:05:14.016
And I love it.


01:05:17.416 --> 01:05:20.711
I remember a little girl


01:05:20.775 --> 01:05:22.499
when I was an intern.


01:05:23.528 --> 01:05:25.666
She came
to the hospital everyday


01:05:25.735 --> 01:05:27.328
to visit her best friend.


01:05:27.399 --> 01:05:31.774
She'd very nearly
drowned in a lake.


01:05:31.847 --> 01:05:34.913
And her friend had
run off to get help


01:05:34.983 --> 01:05:36.260
and there was an accident.


01:05:36.328 --> 01:05:40.551
They'd only just met on vacation.


01:05:40.616 --> 01:05:43.333
They didn't even speak
the same language.


01:05:43.400 --> 01:05:46.247
Yet they were inseparable.


01:05:48.167 --> 01:05:50.339
There was such a bond
between them.


01:05:51.784 --> 01:05:53.671
A strong bond.


01:05:53.736 --> 01:05:56.386
And she came every day.


01:05:56.455 --> 01:05:57.470
Every day.


01:06:02.856 --> 01:06:05.606
She'd hold your hand.


01:06:05.672 --> 01:06:06.948
She had made up her mind


01:06:07.015 --> 01:06:09.187
that she wasn't going
to leave your side.


01:06:09.256 --> 01:06:10.750
And she didn't.


01:06:17.032 --> 01:06:19.366
Why are you telling me this now?


01:06:19.431 --> 01:06:21.122
Why only now?


01:06:21.192 --> 01:06:22.370
I've been here.


01:06:22.440 --> 01:06:26.084
I haven't hidden anything from you.


01:06:26.151 --> 01:06:28.998
I've been right here in front of you
the whole time.


01:06:29.064 --> 01:06:31.617
All you had to do
was open your eyes.


01:06:33.031 --> 01:06:36.828
It was you who questioned me
when I came out of the coma.


01:06:41.032 --> 01:06:44.577
You were the only one
who believed me.


01:06:46.184 --> 01:06:47.842
Yes.


01:07:09.288 --> 01:07:11.906
Kay, where are you?


01:07:15.304 --> 01:07:16.995
<i>Nathan, it's Rachel.</i>


01:07:17.064 --> 01:07:18.493
<i>Everybody here is looking for you.</i>


01:07:18.567 --> 01:07:19.713
<i>Where are you?</i>


01:07:19.783 --> 01:07:21.638
<i>I left six messages</i>
<i>on your cell phone.</i>


01:07:21.703 --> 01:07:24.005
- <i>Will you call me?</i>
<i>- Kay?</i>


01:07:26.120 --> 01:07:27.975
Where are you?
What's wrong with me?


01:07:28.040 --> 01:07:29.698
<i>First of all, don't panic.</i>


01:07:29.767 --> 01:07:32.833
<i>There's a clinic</i>
<i>at the northeast corner</i>


01:07:32.903 --> 01:07:34.791
<i>of 44th and Lexington.</i>


01:07:34.856 --> 01:07:36.798
<i>They'll give you a shot of glucagon.</i>


01:07:36.872 --> 01:07:38.181
- Lexington and what?
- 44th.


01:08:11.367 --> 01:08:13.222
It's okay, Nathan.


01:08:13.287 --> 01:08:15.197
I'm here.


01:08:34.247 --> 01:08:37.825
<i>You're asking me</i>
<i>where we go after we die?</i>


01:08:37.895 --> 01:08:40.743
Nathan, knowing whether
there is an afterlife


01:08:40.807 --> 01:08:42.629
is not the point.


01:08:42.695 --> 01:08:46.852
The important thing is
being alive before you die.


01:08:46.919 --> 01:08:49.701
Today, now.
Fully alive.


01:08:50.663 --> 01:08:53.510
The wonder of life
is in the here and now.


01:08:53.576 --> 01:08:56.259
We always find out too late.


01:09:01.960 --> 01:09:03.967
I've got to go get my daughter,


01:09:04.040 --> 01:09:05.698
and I'm frightened for her.


01:09:05.767 --> 01:09:08.517
So you're going to come with me.


01:09:09.223 --> 01:09:11.078
You're going to come with us.


01:09:11.143 --> 01:09:13.958
This white light, you haven't seen it
on yourself yet, right?


01:09:14.023 --> 01:09:15.300
- No.
- Good.


01:09:15.367 --> 01:09:16.927
That means if you're
on the plane with us


01:09:16.999 --> 01:09:18.755
nothing will happen.


01:09:18.823 --> 01:09:20.252
I don't want to put Tracey in danger.


01:10:14.055 --> 01:10:15.430
Is it him or her?


01:10:41.191 --> 01:10:44.006
This light, what's it like exactly?


01:10:44.071 --> 01:10:45.478
I told you.


01:10:45.544 --> 01:10:48.064
It's like a white halo
shining from the person.


01:10:48.135 --> 01:10:49.826
And you see it all the time?


01:10:49.896 --> 01:10:52.962
No, you only see it once,
and then...


01:10:53.031 --> 01:10:54.241
but that's not what's important.


01:10:54.311 --> 01:10:55.838
I know, I know.


01:11:23.783 --> 01:11:25.922
So who is he anyway?


01:11:25.991 --> 01:11:27.780
- A doctor.
- You work together?


01:11:28.455 --> 01:11:30.495
Not really.
It's kinda complicated.


01:11:31.335 --> 01:11:32.829
He's a friend of yours?


01:11:35.751 --> 01:11:37.312
Why is he here?


01:11:38.535 --> 01:11:39.997
Just traveling with me.


01:11:40.071 --> 01:11:42.656
- I didn't want to travel alone.
- Like Tracey.


01:11:43.431 --> 01:11:45.253
Yeah.
Like Tracey, yeah.


01:11:50.376 --> 01:11:52.350
It's happening tonight?


01:11:52.423 --> 01:11:54.528
Maybe.


01:11:54.599 --> 01:11:56.006
I hope so.


01:11:56.071 --> 01:11:58.210
You can never know in advance.


01:12:47.623 --> 01:12:50.110
You know why I came?
The real reason.


01:12:51.687 --> 01:12:54.654
You came because
you promised her you would.


01:12:55.847 --> 01:12:58.236
You came because
you love your daughter.


01:13:00.167 --> 01:13:02.272
- Don't you?
- Of course I do.


01:13:02.343 --> 01:13:03.870
But there's
something else.


01:13:05.383 --> 01:13:07.009
Naturally.


01:13:07.079 --> 01:13:09.566
Look, Nathan,


01:13:09.639 --> 01:13:11.232
I have a life here


01:13:11.303 --> 01:13:13.507
and I'm trying to build
something solid with Tracey...


01:13:15.111 --> 01:13:16.452
Wait, listen!


01:13:19.623 --> 01:13:23.006
I think I know what
you're trying to tell me


01:13:23.079 --> 01:13:26.756
and I think that we can
avoid this sort of...


01:13:28.967 --> 01:13:30.211
Unpleasantness?


01:13:30.279 --> 01:13:33.094
You know exactly what I mean.


01:13:38.439 --> 01:13:40.000
I want you to come with me.


01:13:40.071 --> 01:13:42.689
I want the three of us
to go back to New York.


01:13:42.759 --> 01:13:44.352
I want you to come home.


01:13:48.391 --> 01:13:50.693
Avoid just that sort of thing.


01:14:52.327 --> 01:14:54.531
Tracey, don't look.


01:15:56.935 --> 01:15:58.659
You go back alone.
I'm staying here.


01:15:58.727 --> 01:16:00.287
I want to stay here.


01:16:00.359 --> 01:16:03.359
- With Tracey?
- Yes, with Tracey, yes.


01:16:04.839 --> 01:16:06.627
- You still need me.
- No.


01:16:06.695 --> 01:16:08.386
I don't know.


01:16:08.455 --> 01:16:10.081
I'm staying, that's all.


01:16:12.807 --> 01:16:16.452
Is there something I should know?


01:16:17.479 --> 01:16:19.235
Something you haven't told me?


01:16:24.007 --> 01:16:25.949
I'm going to miss my plane.


01:16:43.495 --> 01:16:45.982
Honey, do you know how to use it?


01:16:46.055 --> 01:16:48.957
Huh? Press here.
Yes, that's it.


01:16:49.031 --> 01:16:50.689
Good.


01:16:52.807 --> 01:16:54.400
- Daddy?
- Yes.


01:16:54.471 --> 01:16:57.024
The people we saw a while ago...


01:16:57.895 --> 01:16:59.902
- Yes?
- The ones in the accident.


01:16:59.975 --> 01:17:01.698
- Yes?
- The ones who died.


01:17:02.855 --> 01:17:06.946
- Yes.
- Will they have crosses too?


01:17:07.015 --> 01:17:08.160
I don't know.
Maybe.


01:17:11.015 --> 01:17:14.049
But they're not buried
under them, right?


01:17:14.119 --> 01:17:15.166
Who?


01:17:15.239 --> 01:17:16.483
Oh, no.


01:17:18.759 --> 01:17:21.246
But Paul, he's buried
under one, right?


01:17:22.375 --> 01:17:23.520
Yes, honey.


01:17:23.591 --> 01:17:24.868
Listen, honey,


01:17:24.935 --> 01:17:27.423
if anything ever happens to me,


01:17:27.495 --> 01:17:29.437
if I get to feel sick or,
I don't know...


01:17:29.510 --> 01:17:30.754
what do you do?


01:17:30.822 --> 01:17:32.284
- I call Mommy.
- You call Mommy.


01:17:32.359 --> 01:17:33.341
Good, right.


01:17:33.415 --> 01:17:35.716
And who else,
if Mommy isn't there?


01:17:35.783 --> 01:17:37.921
If you have to call for help,
what do you do?


01:17:37.991 --> 01:17:39.846
- I scream.
- You scream?


01:17:39.911 --> 01:17:41.918
Honey, I'm serious.
What do you do?


01:17:41.990 --> 01:17:46.268
I cry?
I know, relax.


01:17:46.343 --> 01:17:47.520
I press here.


01:17:47.591 --> 01:17:49.020
You already showed me.


01:17:50.727 --> 01:17:51.676
Okay.


01:18:30.279 --> 01:18:33.126
Honey,
you remember when...


01:18:33.191 --> 01:18:35.395
when Paul died?


01:18:35.463 --> 01:18:36.870
Do you remember?


01:18:38.503 --> 01:18:40.739
Well, when he died...


01:18:42.439 --> 01:18:44.097
I found a garden slug.


01:18:44.167 --> 01:18:45.411
I remember.


01:18:46.759 --> 01:18:49.148
I remember you asked
a lot of questions.


01:18:49.223 --> 01:18:51.328
Lots and lots of questions.


01:18:51.399 --> 01:18:54.017
Like what?


01:18:54.087 --> 01:18:56.804
You asked us where he was.


01:18:56.870 --> 01:18:58.725
We told you,
"Paul is in heaven.


01:18:58.790 --> 01:19:00.678
In heaven with the angels."


01:19:00.743 --> 01:19:03.939
And you asked us
if you could go see him.


01:19:04.007 --> 01:19:06.428
You wanted to go see him.


01:19:06.503 --> 01:19:09.634
And I don't know
if we always said the right thing.


01:19:10.759 --> 01:19:13.890
- It isn't true?
- What isn't true?


01:19:13.959 --> 01:19:15.551
That Paul's in heaven?


01:19:15.622 --> 01:19:17.084
He could be.


01:19:17.159 --> 01:19:18.369
Maybe.


01:19:18.439 --> 01:19:19.868
But to tell you the truth,


01:19:19.943 --> 01:19:21.252
nobody really knows.
Nobody can know.


01:19:21.319 --> 01:19:23.141
- It's something that...
- I know.


01:19:23.207 --> 01:19:25.029
You do?


01:19:25.095 --> 01:19:28.030
When we die they put us
into the ground...


01:19:28.102 --> 01:19:31.550
and slugs eat us, of course,


01:19:31.623 --> 01:19:33.794
and then we disappear.


01:19:33.862 --> 01:19:35.618
And then we don't exist any more.


01:19:35.687 --> 01:19:38.337
Nobody can be sure of that either.


01:19:39.303 --> 01:19:41.092
But you know,
I believe one thing.


01:19:41.159 --> 01:19:43.647
- Want me to tell you?
- Mm-hmm.


01:19:43.718 --> 01:19:46.020
I think just because we die


01:19:46.086 --> 01:19:49.315
doesn't mean we don't exist anymore.


01:19:49.383 --> 01:19:50.943
Maybe we exist someplace else.


01:19:51.942 --> 01:19:53.087
And you know why I think that?


01:19:56.135 --> 01:19:58.590
When you see a boat vanish...


01:19:58.662 --> 01:20:00.767
have you ever seen a boat
vanish on the horizon?


01:20:02.119 --> 01:20:04.639
When a boat disappears
in the distance,


01:20:04.711 --> 01:20:06.271
it vanishes,


01:20:06.342 --> 01:20:08.797
but does that mean
it doesn't exist anymore?


01:20:08.870 --> 01:20:10.692
No.


01:20:10.759 --> 01:20:12.384
Right.


01:20:12.455 --> 01:20:14.146
I believe dying is like that.


01:20:14.215 --> 01:20:17.150
It's like a boat
vanishing on the horizon.


01:20:17.223 --> 01:20:21.663
Just because you can't see it,
doesn't mean it doesn't exist.


01:23:25.255 --> 01:23:27.459
- Can we talk?
- Why did you come back?


01:23:30.118 --> 01:23:31.809
We didn't want to fly.


01:23:31.879 --> 01:23:34.432
Tracey and I were too scared
to take the plane.


01:23:34.503 --> 01:23:36.739
Besides, I'm in no hurry
to get home.


01:23:37.606 --> 01:23:38.915
So what do you plan to do?


01:23:38.983 --> 01:23:40.990
Here?
I don't know.


01:23:41.063 --> 01:23:41.956
Hang out.


01:23:42.023 --> 01:23:43.932
Spend some time with Tracey.


01:23:44.007 --> 01:23:45.316
Go for walks.


01:23:45.382 --> 01:23:48.000
You could maybe point out
some places to go.


01:23:48.070 --> 01:23:50.405
- Tracey told me you two...
- Places to go?


01:23:51.719 --> 01:23:53.541
Nathan, what's the matter with you?


01:23:53.607 --> 01:23:56.160
- Nothing.
- What do you mean, nothing?


01:23:56.231 --> 01:23:58.719
You call me in the middle
of the night as if...


01:23:58.791 --> 01:24:00.132
I don't know.


01:24:01.798 --> 01:24:04.187
Then you show up two days early
with this strange guy,


01:24:04.263 --> 01:24:05.245
and you come out
with these remarks.


01:24:05.319 --> 01:24:08.319
Now you're talking
about going for walks?


01:24:08.391 --> 01:24:09.852
What's going on?


01:24:09.927 --> 01:24:11.999
You have troubles
at the firm, is that it?


01:24:12.070 --> 01:24:13.412
No, not really.


01:24:13.478 --> 01:24:15.867
Then what?
Are you sick?


01:24:15.942 --> 01:24:18.659
No, not that I'm aware of.


01:24:20.006 --> 01:24:21.250
Not that you're aware of?


01:24:21.318 --> 01:24:22.627
No.


01:24:22.695 --> 01:24:24.582
Just a little hypoglycemia.


01:24:44.071 --> 01:24:45.827
When does it happen?


01:24:49.062 --> 01:24:51.484
Two hours from now,
maybe sooner.


01:24:59.878 --> 01:25:02.464
We had ice cream last night,


01:25:02.534 --> 01:25:04.290
and we talked about Paul.


01:25:05.222 --> 01:25:06.848
On the road
we saw some crosses,


01:25:06.919 --> 01:25:09.057
and afterwards she wanted to...


01:25:11.238 --> 01:25:13.278
does she talk to you about it?


01:25:14.343 --> 01:25:15.936
Not so much these days.


01:25:16.007 --> 01:25:17.184
But is she all right?


01:25:17.254 --> 01:25:18.847
The last time on the phone
when I called,


01:25:18.918 --> 01:25:22.017
- she was already asleep...
- She wasn't asleep.


01:25:23.558 --> 01:25:25.500
She wasn't asleep?


01:25:25.574 --> 01:25:27.330
- No.
- Can't you take a break?


01:25:27.398 --> 01:25:28.608
Five minutes.


01:25:28.678 --> 01:25:31.428
Nathan, in one hour
this flower will be dead.


01:25:31.494 --> 01:25:33.382
It blooms one night a year,
just the once,


01:25:33.447 --> 01:25:36.032
- and I still have...
- Yes, I know that, but...


01:25:38.439 --> 01:25:39.649
sorry.


01:25:49.638 --> 01:25:51.711
When we went home
to New York...


01:25:53.095 --> 01:25:55.167
do you remember
the first thing you did?


01:25:55.238 --> 01:25:57.475
The first.


01:25:59.303 --> 01:26:01.277
You called the office.


01:26:02.630 --> 01:26:04.932
You wanted to know
if anyone had called.


01:26:06.887 --> 01:26:09.156
We'd just buried Paul,


01:26:09.222 --> 01:26:11.611
and you disappeared
into your work.


01:26:14.567 --> 01:26:16.803
You shut yourself off
in your anger.


01:26:16.870 --> 01:26:20.099
But Tracey and I were still there.


01:26:20.166 --> 01:26:21.922
We were alive.


01:26:23.207 --> 01:26:24.865
I know you felt guilty.


01:26:24.935 --> 01:26:26.909
I know that you blamed yourself


01:26:26.982 --> 01:26:28.095
because you heard him cry


01:26:28.167 --> 01:26:29.247
and you didn't go check on him.


01:26:29.319 --> 01:26:31.424
- He called me.
- No.


01:26:32.199 --> 01:26:35.614
Paul cried
and he went back to sleep,


01:26:35.687 --> 01:26:37.475
and even if...


01:26:37.542 --> 01:26:41.187
He called me,
but I didn't go to him.


01:26:41.255 --> 01:26:43.972
Nathan, Paul didn't call anyone.


01:26:45.062 --> 01:26:46.371
Paul's dead.


01:26:46.438 --> 01:26:49.734
I've accepted that and so has Tracey.


01:26:49.798 --> 01:26:51.903
She's accepted it
in her own little way.


01:26:53.094 --> 01:26:55.036
And now you... you need
to accept it too.


01:26:55.110 --> 01:26:57.314
- I'm ready.
- You need to stop...


01:26:58.950 --> 01:27:00.576
I don't know.


01:27:02.215 --> 01:27:03.491
I don't know, Nathan.


01:27:03.558 --> 01:27:05.347
I don't know what to tell you.


01:27:06.598 --> 01:27:11.235
I'm ready.
I came back to tell you.


01:27:12.998 --> 01:27:15.038
And if anything
ever happens to me...


01:27:16.615 --> 01:27:19.397
Why do you say that?


01:27:19.462 --> 01:27:21.796
I wanted you to know
that I've changed.


01:27:41.766 --> 01:27:43.839
I know a river not far from here.


01:27:47.302 --> 01:27:49.790
If you want, I could
show you how to get there.


01:27:49.863 --> 01:27:51.040
Yeah.


01:27:51.110 --> 01:27:52.604
I'd like that.


01:27:53.670 --> 01:27:55.557
A pretty river.


01:27:57.414 --> 01:27:59.040
Right.


01:28:04.550 --> 01:28:07.933
- Not very far?
- No.


01:28:21.478 --> 01:28:24.195
Forgive me.


01:28:53.223 --> 01:28:56.157
<i>Hi, this is Rachel calling</i>
<i>from Nathan's office.</i>


01:28:56.230 --> 01:28:58.172
<i>I'm sorry to bother you, but...</i>


01:28:58.246 --> 01:29:01.726
<i>he's not at home and hasn't been by</i>
<i>the office in several days.</i>


01:29:01.798 --> 01:29:04.002
<i>We can't reach him</i>
<i>on his cell phone either.</i>


01:29:04.070 --> 01:29:07.070
<i>We're worried and thought</i>
<i>maybe you'd heard from him.</i>


01:29:07.142 --> 01:29:09.630
<i>Could you please call us</i>
<i>if you've got any news?</i>


01:29:39.302 --> 01:29:41.091
They're looking for you.


01:29:43.494 --> 01:29:45.633
Yes, I know.


01:30:07.238 --> 01:30:08.864
<i>"Someone once told me,</i>


01:30:08.934 --> 01:30:12.414
<i>"'The wonder of life is</i>
<i>in the here and now. '


01:30:13.798 --> 01:30:15.708
<i>"I'm going to die soon.</i>


01:30:16.998 --> 01:30:20.577
<i>"And yet, I'm no longer</i>
<i>dominated by fear.</i>


01:30:24.102 --> 01:30:26.949
<i>"Life is full of riches...</i>


01:30:27.014 --> 01:30:28.901
<i>"the gestures, the laughter,</i>


01:30:28.966 --> 01:30:30.941
<i>"the joy we shared.</i>


01:30:32.166 --> 01:30:34.173
<i>"I remember it all.</i>


01:30:39.558 --> 01:30:41.663
<i>"I remember your breathing too,</i>


01:30:41.734 --> 01:30:43.043
<i>"when you slept in the car.</i>


01:30:43.110 --> 01:30:45.860
<i>"Mommy's face when she saw us.</i>


01:30:45.926 --> 01:30:48.097
<i>"We did a lot of things together.</i>


01:30:48.166 --> 01:30:49.922
<i>Lots and lots of things. "


01:30:52.614 --> 01:30:54.403
<i>"I've learned a lot.</i>


01:30:55.526 --> 01:30:58.046
<i>I've met some wonderful people. "


01:30:59.046 --> 01:31:01.664
Hi, I-I'm Jennifer.


01:31:14.214 --> 01:31:16.353
<i>"Cherish your happiness.</i>


01:31:16.422 --> 01:31:18.975
<i>"Savor it at every instant.</i>


01:31:21.542 --> 01:31:22.786
<i>"And above all,</i>


01:31:22.854 --> 01:31:25.603
<i>"don't get upset if you think of me.</i>


01:31:26.758 --> 01:31:27.652
<i>"Don't be sad.</i>


01:31:46.854 --> 01:31:49.472
<i>"And one day,</i>
<i>if you want to talk to me...</i>


01:31:49.542 --> 01:31:51.876
<i>"if you really want to...</i>


01:31:51.942 --> 01:31:53.600
<i>"pick a spot you like.</i>


01:31:53.670 --> 01:31:56.539
<i>"A spot where we used</i>
<i>to go together.</i>


01:31:59.718 --> 01:32:02.337
<i>"You'll be able</i>
<i>to talk to me... you'll see.</i>


01:32:03.782 --> 01:32:05.637
<i>"Because I'll be there.</i>


01:32:15.334 --> 01:32:16.709
<i>"And remember,</i>


01:32:16.774 --> 01:32:20.352
<i>"don't be ashamed to tell people</i>
<i>you care about</i>


01:32:20.422 --> 01:32:21.949
<i>"that you love them.</i>


01:32:23.526 --> 01:32:26.875
<i>I love you both very much. "


01:32:49.318 --> 01:32:51.293
Did you sleep well?


01:32:51.366 --> 01:32:52.478
Yes.


01:32:54.438 --> 01:32:56.707
Want me to make you a fresh pot?


01:32:56.774 --> 01:32:58.367
No, it's okay.


01:34:09.094 --> 01:34:11.134
I need to see you.
You've got to get out here.


01:34:11.206 --> 01:34:12.929
I need to see you now,
understand?


01:34:12.998 --> 01:34:14.973
- <i>I'm here.</i>
<i>- Take the first flight...</i>


01:34:15.046 --> 01:34:16.955
<i>I'm here.</i>
<i>I'm here with you.</i>


01:34:17.030 --> 01:34:18.623
What do you mean here?


01:34:18.694 --> 01:34:21.563
<i>On the road to the airport...</i>
<i>the Crossroads Motel.</i>


01:34:21.638 --> 01:34:23.198
<i>I'm here.</i>


01:34:23.269 --> 01:34:25.309
<i>I'll wait for you here.</i>


01:35:05.798 --> 01:35:07.456
You lied to me from the start.


01:35:07.526 --> 01:35:08.770
No.


01:35:08.838 --> 01:35:10.300
You said it was me.


01:35:10.374 --> 01:35:11.551
You said so.


01:35:12.741 --> 01:35:15.294
You said I was the one
who was going to die.


01:35:15.365 --> 01:35:18.365
So what did I see?
Tell me.


01:35:18.438 --> 01:35:20.577
I was the one who
was supposed to die.


01:35:20.646 --> 01:35:22.173
It was supposed to be me!


01:35:22.246 --> 01:35:24.034
You said so!


01:35:24.101 --> 01:35:26.240
No.


01:35:29.478 --> 01:35:31.387
Nathan?


01:35:38.950 --> 01:35:40.292
Tracey, have you seen daddy?


01:35:40.358 --> 01:35:41.536
No.


01:36:04.646 --> 01:36:06.206
I'm a Messenger, right?


01:36:08.198 --> 01:36:09.605
Yes.


01:36:10.758 --> 01:36:12.830
And my wife is going to die.


01:36:15.462 --> 01:36:17.185
Yes.


01:36:17.254 --> 01:36:18.498
Why didn't you tell me


01:36:18.566 --> 01:36:20.671
when you came to see me
the first time


01:36:20.741 --> 01:36:22.716
instead of being so mysterious.


01:36:22.790 --> 01:36:25.124
The swan's song and all that bullshit.


01:36:25.189 --> 01:36:26.564
You wouldn't have believed me.


01:36:26.630 --> 01:36:28.037
You never would have believed me.


01:36:28.102 --> 01:36:29.891
I was trying to prepare you.


01:36:29.958 --> 01:36:31.518
Prepare me for what?


01:36:31.590 --> 01:36:33.630
You're a Messenger.


01:36:33.702 --> 01:36:35.196
A teacher of life.


01:36:35.270 --> 01:36:36.993
But to be a teacher of life


01:36:37.061 --> 01:36:39.647
you have to remember
your own mortality.


01:36:39.718 --> 01:36:42.565
- You have to.
- But why does she have to die?


01:36:42.629 --> 01:36:43.611
Why her?


01:36:44.358 --> 01:36:47.838
All Messengers lose
the person closest to them.


01:36:49.670 --> 01:36:52.452
That's the price...
the price of grace.


01:36:53.478 --> 01:36:54.820
I paid the same price.


01:36:54.886 --> 01:36:56.260
But in time,


01:36:56.325 --> 01:36:58.911
you'll know that you
were there until the very end.


01:36:58.982 --> 01:37:00.989
Through the very end.


01:37:02.310 --> 01:37:04.285
That's the price
of becoming a Messenger.


01:37:04.357 --> 01:37:06.113
But I never asked for this.


01:37:06.182 --> 01:37:08.091
Nobody ever gave me a choice.


01:37:09.574 --> 01:37:11.199
You made your choice, Nathan.


01:37:11.269 --> 01:37:13.658
You made your choice
when you decided to come back


01:37:13.734 --> 01:37:15.806
after you had died on that road.


01:37:15.877 --> 01:37:17.252
And you came back.


01:37:17.318 --> 01:37:19.009
And now you know why.


01:37:19.078 --> 01:37:20.933
What brought you back?


01:37:22.886 --> 01:37:24.348
A face.


01:37:24.422 --> 01:37:25.534
Whose face?


01:37:27.845 --> 01:37:29.471
Claire's face.


01:37:32.262 --> 01:37:33.920
<i>She was afraid.</i>


01:37:36.293 --> 01:37:38.082
<i>She needed me.</i>


01:38:28.837 --> 01:38:30.212
Where were you?


01:38:32.933 --> 01:38:34.559
I got lost.


01:38:37.221 --> 01:38:38.748
We were waiting for you.


01:38:39.589 --> 01:38:41.280
I got lost.


01:38:44.805 --> 01:38:46.845
We thought that you'd left us...


01:38:48.806 --> 01:38:51.172
that you'd...


01:38:54.630 --> 01:38:57.630
- We were worried.
- I know.


01:38:59.045 --> 01:39:01.314
But don't be scared.


01:39:01.381 --> 01:39:03.137
I'm here now.


01:39:04.709 --> 01:39:06.848
I'll never leave you again.


01:39:12.870 --> 01:39:14.844
I'm here.


01:43:31.663 --> 01:43:32.663
Subtitles by LeapinLar

